The Human Genome Project was enabled by computational methods developed for NASA data processing.
GPS — used in every smartphone, supply chain, and self-driving car — is a direct product of space programme investment.
The James Webb Space Telescope has already revolutionised our understanding of the early universe, galaxy formation, and the atmospheric composition of exoplanets.
Over 2,000 NASA spinoff technologies are in commercial use, including memory foam, scratch-resistant coatings, and advances in water purification.
